E AX3033 600-macro-rule-unreachable.ax:21:8-12 macro-unreachable-rule "macro `defU` has a rule that can never match: rule 2 is shadowed by rule 1" !"rules are tried IN ORDER and the first whose pattern matches wins (macro-system.md MAC-LANG-18); an earlier rule of the same arity whose elements are all plain binders matches every invocation of that arity, so nothing of that arity after it is reachable" ?"give the earlier rule a pattern that can FAIL - a literal, or a parenthesised shape of two or more elements - or delete this one. A one-element `(p)` is the bare binder `p`: the parentheses are the same ones an argument loses, so it still matches everything"
